      "name": "AllocateCelImageBuffer",
      "signature": "void AllocateCelImageBuffer(uint * pCelHeader, uint * * ppOutput, uint * pdwSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Allocates and serializes a cel image buffer from a cel file header.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate CELFILE_SERIALIZED flag (dwFlags & 0x1) is set\n2. Validate cel file version equals 5\n3. Set CELFILE_PROCESSED flag (dwFlags |= 0x2)\n4. Convert relative frame offsets to absolute pointers (pCelHeader + offset)\n5. For each frame, fix up palette pointer if present (offset 0x20)\n6. Calculate total buffer size: header (0x18) + cel count * 4 + frame data\n7. Allocate output buffer via AllocClientMemory\n8. Initialize buffer header: magic=6, flags (1 or 5), dimensions\n9. Copy frame data: flags, dimensions, palette info, pixel data\n10. Copy palette data if present\n11. Store output buffer pointer and size to output parameters\n\nParameters:\n- pCelHeader (uint*): Source cel file header, must have CELFILE_SERIALIZED flag\n- ppOutput (uint**): Output pointer to receive allocated buffer\n- pdwSize (uint*): Output pointer to receive buffer size in bytes\n\nReturns:\n- void: Terminates process on validation failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1: CELFILE_SERIALIZED flag\n- 0x2: CELFILE_PROCESSED flag (set after processing)\n- 0x4: CELFILE_24BIT flag (determines output flags 1 vs 5)\n- 0x5: Required cel file version\n- 0x6: Output buffer magic signature\n- 0x18 (24): Buffer header size\n- 0x23 (35): Frame header overhead per cel\n- 0x34 (52): Offset to frame pointer array in cel header\n- 0x2B9 (697): Line number for serialized flag assertion\n- 0x2BA (698): Line number for version assertion\n- 0x2D1 (721): Line number for allocation\n\nRelated Functions:\n- AllocClientMemory: Allocates memory from heap\n- FogAssertFail: Logs assertion failure\n- TerminateProcessWithCode: Exits process with code",
