      "name": "ClearCelGraphicsCache",
      "signature": "dword ClearCelGraphicsCache(CelFile * pCelFile)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Validates CEL file structure and clears cell graphics cache.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Verify input CEL file pointer not NULL; return 0 on null\n2. Check if CEL type field (offset +0x00) equals 6 (CELFILE_VER)\n3. Validate CEL data pointer at offset +0x18 is not NULL\n4. Calculate total cells = width * height\n5. Loop through each cell index from 0 to count-1\n6. For each cell, check data pointer at offset +0x18\n7. If cell pointer non-NULL and data valid, invoke callback if registered\n8. Clear graphics reference by writing 0x00000000 to offset +0x18\n9. Call Ordinal_10043(0x5ff, 0) for palette update\n10. Return 1 on successful cache clear\n\nParameters:\n- pCelFile (CelFile*): Pointer to CEL file structure\n  Offset +0x00: Type field (must equal 6)\n  Offset +0x10: Width (cell count X dimension)\n  Offset +0x14: Height (cell count Y dimension)\n  Offset +0x18: Pointer to first cell data element\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Cache clear succeeded, all graphics references cleared\n- 0: NULL input pointer provided\n- Does not return: Asserts on type mismatch or NULL data pointer\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x6: CELFILE_VER constant for validation\n- 0x5ff (1535): Palette update command code\n- 0x5d3 (1491): Assert line for version mismatch\n- 0x5d7 (1495): Assert line for NULL parent pointer",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:5cb95fecf22a4e25fd97865dde0d3d5b",
