      "comment": "Cleanup and destroy a resource container by processing cleanup callbacks and destroying all contained lists.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear field at offset +0x10 (field 4 in structure)\n2. Process items in pContainer[3] by calling FUN_6fe136a0 with each entry from pContainer[1]\n3. Iterate pContainer[6] callback entries, calling function pointer at field 0 with item value from field 8\n4. Destroy pContainer[0x10] list by calling FUN_6fe138f0 then Ordinal_403 (SMemFree) for each entry\n5. Destroy pContainer[0xc] list by calling FUN_6fe132f0 then Ordinal_403 (SMemFree) for each entry\n\nParameters:\npContainer: undefined4 * - Pointer to resource container structure with cleanup fields\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nStructure Layout (Container):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x00   | 4    | vtable     | void* | Virtual function table (function pointer)\n0x04   | 4    | listStart  | void* | Start of first item list\n0x08   | 4    | unknown1   | void* | Unknown field\n0x0c   | 4    | listTail   | int   | Tail/count of second list\n0x10   | 4    | field4     | int   | Cleared at start\n0x18   | 4    | count      | int   | Count of callback entries\n0x1c   | 4    | cbArray    | void* | Callback array with 0xc-byte entries\n0x30   | 4    | list2Tail  | int   | Second list tail/count\n0x40   | 4    | list1Head  | int   | First list head\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x0c: Stride in callback array (12 bytes per entry)\n0xfffffffe: Special code passed to Ordinal_403 for cleanup\n\nNote: Function uses compiler temporaries (iVar1, iVar3 for loop values, uVar2 for iteration index) optimized away in register allocation.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
