      "name": "DestructorWithConditionalCleanup",
      "signature": "void * DestructorWithConditionalCleanup(void * this, void * pThis, byte fDeleteCallback)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "Destructor with conditional callback invocation based on flag\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Invoke FUN_6fe132f0 preprocessing on this pointer\n2. Check if fDeleteCallback flag has bit 0x01 set\n3. If flag set AND this pointer non-NULL, invoke Ordinal_403 (D2Common - likely destructor callback)\n4. Return the this pointer\n\nParameters:\n- this: void pointer to object being destructed (IMPLICIT in ECX register via __thiscall)\n- fDeleteCallback: byte flag where bit 0x01 triggers destruction callback (0x01=delete, 0x00=skip)\n\nReturns:\n- void pointer to the original object (returned in EAX)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If fDeleteCallback bit 0x01 is clear, callback is skipped\n- If this pointer is NULL, callback invocation is skipped regardless of flag state\n- FUN_6fe132f0 is always called first before any conditional logic\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x01: Bit mask for controlling deletion callback behavior\n- 0xFFFFFFFF: Sentinel/magic value passed to Ordinal_403 (context-dependent)\n- 0x00: Null terminator parameter for Ordinal_403",
