      "name": "DestructorWithOptionalDelete",
      "signature": "void * DestructorWithOptionalDelete(void * this, byte bDelete)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "Destructor with conditional cleanup. Calls cleanup routine, then optionally deletes object via Storm memory free if delete flag is set.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call cleanup routine on this pointer\n2. Check if delete flag (0x01 bit) is set in bDelete parameter\n3. If flag set AND this pointer non-null, call SMemFree to deallocate\n4. Return this pointer\n\nParameters:\n  this - Object pointer (ECX implicit, __thiscall)\n  bDelete - Deletion flag byte (bit 0 = delete flag, 0 = cleanup only, 1 = cleanup and delete)\n\nReturns:\n  void * - Returns this pointer (object address in EAX)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If this is NULL, SMemFree is skipped (safety check at 0x6fe12f71)\n  - Delete flag check uses bitwise AND with 0x1 to extract delete bit\n  - Uses Storm.dll SMemFree (Ordinal 403) for deallocation",
