      "name": "CleanupAuctionSlots",
      "signature": "void CleanupAuctionSlots(void * pAuctionData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Cleanup and destroy all active auction slot data structures.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize SEH exception handler frame with pointer to LAB_6fe29225\n2. Set vftable to PTR_ProcessAuctionSlot_6fe2c90c\n3. Process list at offset 0x40 (param_1[0x10]): Call FUN_6fe138f0 for each element, then Ordinal_403 to destroy\n4. Process list at offset 0x30 (param_1[0xc]): Call FUN_6fe132f0 for each element, then Ordinal_403 to destroy\n5. Iterate list at offset 0x38+0x4 (param_1[0xf]): For each non-zero head, call FUN_6fe136a0 on (base + count)\n6. If head non-null: allocate node via FUN_6fe13b10, link structures, zero pointers\n7. Iterate list at offset 0x28+0x4 (param_1[0xb]): Similar cleanup as step 5-6\n8. Set vftable to PTR_ProcessAuctionSlot_6fe2c8fc, zero param_1[4]\n9. Call FUN_6fe13870 on param_1[1] (inner structure)\n10. Process array at offset 0x1c: Iterate param_1[6] times with stride 0xc, call FUN_6fe13850 on each element, then FUN_6fe136a0\n11. Call FUN_6fe134c0 on param_1[5] (cleanup auxiliary data)\n12. Call FUN_6fe13870 on param_1[1] again\n13. Call FUN_6fe136a0 on param_1[2] (cleanup final structure)\n14. Restore exception handler and return\n\nParameters:\npAuctionData (void *, IMPLICIT) - pointer to auction data structure containing lists and arrays to destroy\n\nReturns:\nvoid",
