      "name": "DestroyWithOptionalFreeing",
      "signature": "void * DestroyWithOptionalFreeing(void * this, byte fFreeMemory)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "Destructor that conditionally frees memory for object\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Trigger fatal error handler on this pointer (validate/cleanup)\n2. Check if fFreeMemory flag (bit 0) is set AND this pointer is non-null\n3. If both conditions true, call SMemFree to deallocate memory with flags\n4. Return this pointer (allows chaining)\n\nParameters:\n- this (ECX, IMPLICIT): Pointer to object to destroy\n- fFreeMemory (byte): Flag where bit 0 indicates whether to free memory (0x01 = free, 0x00 = keep)\n\nReturns:\n- void*: Returns the this pointer (same as input), allowing for chaining or post-destruction access\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If fFreeMemory flag bit 0 is clear (even), memory is not freed (only error handler called)\n- If this pointer is NULL, memory freeing is skipped even if flag is set\n- String \"delete\" is passed to SMemFree with 0xFFFFFFFF and 0x00000000 parameters",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:971e52ca170c736a7516f041b09754b4",
