      "name": "DestructorExceptionList",
      "signature": "void DestructorExceptionList(ExceptionListFrame * pExceptionFrame)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Destructor for C++ exception list, properly unwinding and freeing all exception nodes. Calls Ordinal_403 for container destruction.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set up exception handler frame (SEH) with __fastcall parameter in ECX\n2. Initialize exception context by saving current ExceptionList and setting new frame\n3. Loop through each slot in exception array (dwIndex = 0 to count-1):\n   a. Calculate slot pointer = array_base + (dwIndex * 0xc)\n   b. Set dwState to 0 (active destruction phase)\n   c. Inner loop: while slot item count > 0:\n      - Call FUN_6fe13b40 with item count and first element pointer\n      - Call FUN_6fe136a0 on returned pointer for cleanup\n      - Repeat until count exhausted\n   d. Set dwState to 0xffffffff (frame completion marker)\n   e. Call FUN_6fe136a0 on (slot+1) pointer\n   f. Increment dwIndex counter\n   g. Add 0xc to offset for next slot\n4. Restore ExceptionList pointer from saved context\n5. If array base pointer is non-null:\n   - Call Ordinal_403 with array base, type descriptor, and completion flags (calls __delDtor destructor)\n6. Final exception list restoration\n7. Return\n\nParameters:\n- pExceptionFrame (ExceptionListFrame *): Pointer to exception frame structure\n  [+0x4]: uint - Count of exception slots to unwind\n  [+0x8]: void* - Array base pointer of exception nodes (12 bytes each)\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value, function performs cleanup and state restoration\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Zero slot count: Entire main loop skipped, only array cleanup performed\n- Null array pointer: Array cleanup (Ordinal_403) skipped entirely\n- dwState flags: 0 = active destruction, 0xffffffff = frame boundary marker\n- Slot stride: 0xc (12 bytes per node in array)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fe13b40: Extract item from exception node for destruction\n- FUN_6fe136a0: Item cleanup/destructor handler\n- Ordinal_403: Container destructor via type descriptor",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:4fa45e51f3ceaf8c504825f9cef7e4ae",
