      "name": "DestructorWithOptionalCleanup",
      "signature": "void * DestructorWithOptionalCleanup(void * this, byte bCleanupFlag)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "Destructor with conditional cleanup - handles base cleanup and optional memory deallocation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_6fe13540 with this pointer (perform base cleanup of object)\n2. Test cleanup flag parameter for bit 0 set (memory deallocation requested)\n3. Verify this pointer is not NULL (non-zero address check)\n4. If cleanup bit is set AND pointer is valid: call SMemFree (Ordinal_403)\n5. SMemFree call parameters: pObject, \"delete\" string, 0xffffffff flags, 0\n6. Return this pointer unchanged for method chaining or stack cleanup\n\nParameters:\n  bCleanupFlag: Cleanup control flag (byte), bit 0 controls SMemFree invocation\n\nReturns:\n  void*: Returns input this pointer unchanged (always non-NULL if function entered)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If cleanup flag bit 0 is clear: performs base cleanup only, skips deallocation\n  - If this pointer is NULL: base cleanup still called, but SMemFree skipped for safety\n  - __thiscall calling convention: this pointer implicit in ECX, cleanup flag on stack\n  - Function appears to be virtual destructor for COM-style object hierarchy",
