      "signature": "int * DestroyNodeWithCleanup(void * this, int * pNode, byte fInvokeCallback)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "Destroy a node and optionally invoke cleanup callback.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Unlink and close the node via UnlinkAndCloseNode\n2. Test if fInvokeCallback flag (bit 0) is set\n3. If callback flag set and pNode is non-null, invoke Ordinal_403 (delete/destructor callback)\n4. Return the node pointer (pNode)\n\nParameters:\n- pNode (int *): Pointer to node structure to destroy. Used as this pointer (ECX).\n- fInvokeCallback (byte): Flag byte. Bit 0 (0x01) determines if cleanup callback invoked.\n\nReturns:\n- int *: The node pointer (pNode) passed in.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If fInvokeCallback bit 0 is clear, only UnlinkAndCloseNode is called, callback skipped\n- If pNode is NULL and callback flag set, callback is NOT invoked (NULL check prevents it)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x01: Callback flag bit mask\n- 0xffffffff: Special parameter for Ordinal_403 (likely all bits set flag)\n- 0x00: Zero parameter for Ordinal_403 (likely disable flag)\n- \"delete\": String constant passed to Ordinal_403 callback\n\nRelated Functions:\n- UnlinkAndCloseNode: Performs node unlink/close operations first\n- Ordinal_403: Destructor/cleanup callback handler (Storm.dll or similar)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:971e52ca170c736a7516f041b09754b4",
