      "name": "CleanupSpriteDecompressionLock",
      "signature": "void CleanupSpriteDecompressionLock(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Cleanup and delete sprite decompression synchronization lock if initialized.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if g_dwSpriteDecompressionLockInitialized flag is set (non-zero)\n2. If initialized: Enter critical section at g_hSpriteDecompressionLock to synchronize\n3. Clear g_dwSpriteDecompressionLockInitialized flag to 0\n4. Delete critical section object to free resources\n5. Return (no return value)\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Always succeeds, returns regardless of lock initialization state\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If lock not initialized (flag == 0), function returns immediately without entering section\n- Called during module cleanup/shutdown sequence\n- Must be synchronized before calling to prevent race conditions\n\nRelated Functions:\n- InitializeSpriteDecompressionLock() - Creates and initializes the lock\n- Ordinal_10053 - Module shutdown handler that calls this cleanup routine",
