      "name": "DecompressImageData",
      "signature": "void DecompressImageData(byte * pbSrc, byte * pbDest, int nLines, int nWidth, int nTableOffset, int nTableIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Decompresses encoded image data using table-based transformation with per-line processing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize line buffer pointer to destination + line width\n2. For each source line:\n   a. Read control byte from source\n   b. Extract lower 3 bits (dwBitMask) for unrolled case count\n   c. Extract upper 5 bits (nChunkCount) for main loop iterations\n   d. Process remainder bytes via switch/case fallthrough (0-7 bytes)\n   e. Process main loop in 8-byte chunks (nChunkCount iterations)\n   f. For each byte, read lookup table at [nTableOffset + byte] and index with nTableIndex\n   g. Update destination: (dest_byte * 256) + table_value\n   h. Check high bit of control byte (0x80) for continuation\n   i. If set, advance and loop back to step 2a\n   j. Otherwise move to next line and decrement line count\n3. Return when all lines processed\n\nParameters:\npbSrc - Source encoded data buffer (control + index bytes)\npbDest - Destination decompressed image buffer\nnLines - Number of scanlines to process\nnWidth - Bytes per scanline (line stride)\nnTableOffset - Offset to lookup table in memory\nnTableIndex - Secondary index into lookup table\n\nReturns:\nNothing (void). Destination buffer filled with decompressed image data.\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x07 - Bit mask for control byte low bits (7 = 3 bits)\n0x80 - High bit set in control byte indicates line continuation\n0x100 - Multiplication factor for accumulating table values (256)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Switch/case fallthrough processes 0-7 remainder bytes before main loop\n- High bit check on control byte determines if next control byte reads from continuation\n- Unaligned reads due to variable-length control bytes and byte-wise data access\n- Table lookup combines two offsets: nTableOffset and nTableIndex for 2D table access",
