      "name": "CopyDataWithIndirection",
      "signature": "void CopyDataWithIndirection(byte * pbSourceIndices, byte * pbDestination, int nIterations, int nRowSize, int nBaseOffset)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Copy data using indirect byte indexing with row-based alignment optimization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize row pointer to destination + row offset\n2. Read control byte from source indices, increment source pointer\n3. Check if control byte negative: if yes, extract alignment (bits 0-2) and chunk count (bits 3-7)\n4. Process unaligned lead bytes (1-7 bytes) using switch statement fall-through\n5. For each byte in unaligned portion: read byte from source[index], add base offset, write to dest[offset]\n6. Advance both source and destination by alignment count\n7. Loop through chunk count, processing 8 bytes per iteration (two unrolled MOVs per byte)\n8. Check if low 7 bits of control byte non-zero: if yes, advance destination and repeat from step 2\n9. Decrement row iteration counter; if zero, return; otherwise advance to next row and repeat\n\nParameters:\n- pbSourceIndices (byte *): IMPLICIT ECX - control/index byte stream\n- pbDestination (byte *): IMPLICIT EDX - output buffer (modified in-place)\n- nIterations (int): Stack[0x4] - number of rows to process\n- nRowSize (int): Stack[0x8] - bytes to advance destination per row\n- nBaseOffset (int): Stack[0xc] - base address for indirect indexing lookup\n\nReturns:\n- void (result in modified pbDestination buffer)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Control byte < 0: Marks valid processing block (high bit distinguishes from end-of-row marker)\n- Control byte & 0x7f == 0: Signals end of current row, move to next row chunk\n- Unaligned handling: 0-7 bytes before main 8-byte chunk loop via switch fall-through\n- 8-byte chunks: Fully unrolled loop for maximum throughput",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:ac6111f4ea8617081b83fe0914a01a43",
