      "name": "DecodeCelImageLines",
      "signature": "void DecodeCelImageLines(byte * pCelHeader, byte * pbDest, byte * pbClipStart, int nClipLeft, int nClipRight, uint dwStride, byte * pLinesToSkip, int nLinesToDraw, byte * pbPalette, dword dwBlendTable, dword dwColorTable)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Decodes RLE-compressed CEL image lines to destination buffer with optional clipping and color transforms.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate dwStride >= header width and nLinesToSkip + nLinesToDraw <= header height\n2. Skip source data for nLinesToSkip lines (parse RLE opcodes without output)\n3. Check header flag bit 0: if clear, negate stride for bottom-up rendering\n4. If g_dwGameRunning != 0: use inline pixel loops with clipping per-pixel\n5. If g_dwGameRunning == 0: dispatch to optimized helper functions based on transform mode\n6. Decode each line: high bit=0 means copy N pixels, high bit=1 means skip (N & 0x7F) transparent pixels, N=0 ends line\n\nParameters:\n- pCelHeader (byte*): CEL header at +0x4=width, +0x8=height, +0x20=RLE data start\n- pbDest (byte*): Destination pixel buffer\n- pbClipStart (byte*): Current X position for clipping (reused as line tracker in decode)\n- nClipLeft (int): Left clip boundary (0=no clipping)\n- nClipRight (int): Right clip boundary (0=no clipping)\n- dwStride (int): Bytes per destination row (negated internally for bottom-up)\n- pLinesToSkip (byte*): Number of lines to skip (cast from int)\n- nLinesToDraw (int): Number of lines to render\n- pbPalette (byte*): Optional 256-byte palette lookup table\n- dwBlendTable (dword): Optional 256x256 alpha blend table address\n- dwColorTable (dword): Optional 256-byte color remap table address\n\nReturns:\n- void (renders directly to pbDest)\n\nRendering Modes (based on NULL checks):\n- pbPalette && dwBlendTable: palette + alpha blend\n- pbPalette && dwColorTable: palette + color remap\n- pbPalette only: simple palette lookup\n- dwColorTable && dwBlendTable: dual table transform\n- dwColorTable only: color remap\n- dwBlendTable only: alpha blend with dest\n- none: direct copy\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20 (32): Offset to RLE data in CEL header\n- 0x7F (127): Mask for transparent pixel count\n- 0x100 (256): Stride for 256x256 blend table lookup",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:d715c715e9069524e0bffeceeead6880",
