      "name": "ZeroBufferDwords",
      "signature": "void ZeroBufferDwords(dword * pdwBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Zero-fill a 0x4000 DWORD buffer using REP STOSD\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Move buffer pointer from ECX to EDI (fastcall uses ECX for first param)\n2. Load count 0x4000 into ECX\n3. Zero EAX\n4. Execute REP STOSD to store zero dwords and auto-advance EDI\n\nParameters:\n  pdwBuffer (uint *) - IMPLICIT in ECX: pointer to DWORD buffer to zero (at least 16384 DWORDs)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Assumes buffer is aligned and large enough for 16384 DWORDs (65536 bytes)\n  - Uses fastcall convention with buffer pointer in ECX register\n  - REP STOSD is more efficient than loop-based clearing\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x4000 - buffer size in DWORDs (16384 DWORDs = 65536 bytes)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:9e20ea0b749b6a6baa3c5bb158fff5cf",
