      "name": "ComputeResourceHash",
      "signature": "uint ComputeResourceHash(int nResourceId, byte * pbData, int * pdwHashResult, dword * pdwExtra)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Compute hash value for resource based on type and data offsets.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_6fe18fb0 with resource ID and data pointer to compute initial hash\n2. Store initial hash in output parameter\n3. Read resource type from offset 0x20\n4. If type=6 with flag 0x02 set, OR type=3, OR type=4:\n   a. Verify resource context pointer at offset 0x44 is non-null\n   b. If null, assert failure (non-returning)\n   c. Call Ordinal_502 (Storm.dll cache function) with context and flags (1, 0)\n   d. Retrieve stored hash from output parameter\n5. Otherwise, sum offsets 0x30, 0x34, 0x38, 0x3c, 0x40 from resource ID\n6. Add summed offsets to hash value\n7. Apply XOR-based mixing: extract bits and XOR with rotated values\n8. Return final mixed hash\n\nParameters:\nnResourceId (int) - Resource ID or pointer to resource structure\npbData (byte*) - Pointer to resource data buffer\npdwHashResult (uint*) - Output pointer for computed hash value\npdwExtra (uint*) - IMPLICIT (in EDX) - Extra parameter or context\n\nReturns:\nuint - Final mixed hash value (used for cache lookups or validation)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Type 6 requires 0x02 flag set to trigger cache lookup\n- Assertion failure with non-returning FUN_6fe21293 on null context\n- Hash mixing uses 13-bit shifted XOR patterns (0x1fff masks)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20, 0x1c, 0x44, 0x40, 0x3c, 0x38, 0x34, 0x30 - Offsets in resource structure\n- 0x02 - Flag mask for type 6 check\n- 0x1fff0000, 0x1fff00, 0x1fff - XOR mixing masks\n- 0x1, 0x0 - Parameters to Ordinal_502",
