      "name": "SetByteSwapResult",
      "signature": "void SetByteSwapResult(dword dwValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Store byte swap operation result to global state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load parameter dwValue from stack [ESP + 0x4]\n2. Store value into global g_dwByteSwapResult variable (0x6feb6ab4)\n3. Execute RET 0x4 instruction, returning to caller and cleaning up parameter\n\nParameters:\ndwValue - 32-bit unsigned integer containing result code from byte swap operation (typically 0 for success or non-zero for error status)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; function modifies global state only\n\nNotes:\nOrdinal 10011 is likely D2Common module function for internal state management",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
