      "name": "InitializeCompressedGameData",
      "signature": "void InitializeCompressedGameData(int nInitialize)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initialize or cleanup compressed game data structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_423 (LoadCompressedData) with \"Diablo II\" context and data label\n2. Pass target pointer address 0x6fe3011c for storing result\n3. Read nInitialize parameter from stack\n4. If nInitialize is zero (cleanup request), clear g_pGameStructurePtr to NULL\n5. Return to caller with stack cleanup (RET 0x4)\n\nParameters:\n- nInitialize (int): Non-zero to initialize/retain; zero to cleanup\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Ordinal_423 always called regardless of nInitialize value\n- Cleanup only sets pointer to NULL, does not call deallocator\n- g_pGameStructurePtr is global shared with other functions",
