      "name": "InitiateCelGraphicsBlock",
      "signature": "int InitiateCelGraphicsBlock(CelFileInfo * pcelFile)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initiate or update sprite CEL graphics block for a game unit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameter (pcelFile) - assert if NULL\n2. Check if CEL file already loaded (pcelFile->tableIndex != 0):\n   a. If loaded: call GetCelDataByIndex to reinitialize and set pcelFile->padding0\n   b. Return 1 (success)\n3. If not loaded (uninitialized CEL file):\n   a. Initialize two 0x103-byte buffers with zeros via REP STOSD\n   b. Call LoadOrInitializeSpriteCelData to load CEL data into buffer\n   c. Call FindMatchingTableEntry with hash table 0x6fef2bc0\n   d. If found entry: check flag byte at [entry+0x20][0x20] & 0x01\n      - If set: OR pcelFile[1].tableIndex with 0x04 (mark as initialized)\n      - Return 1 (success)\n   e. If not found and conditions met (dwHashIndexB > 1 AND dwHashIndexA != 0 AND !(pbUnused & 0x01)):\n      - Calculate scaled CEL index via ConvertDirectionToNormalized8bit with unit dimension >> 6\n      - Adjust dwCelIndex based on CEL data stride (divide by stride if > 2)\n      - Retry FindMatchingTableEntry with updated index\n      - Assert if not found on retry (file offset 0x69a)\n      - Assert if dwHashIndexA still != 0 (file offset 0x69b)\n4. Call InitializeSpriteGraphicsBlock to build graphics data structures\n5. Return result from InitializeSpriteGraphicsBlock\n\nParameters:\n- pcelFile (CelFileInfo*): CEL file info structure containing tableIndex, height, width fields\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Success (entry found or newly initialized)\n- 0: Failure (only if InitializeSpriteGraphicsBlock fails)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x6fef2bc0: Graphics hash table base address\n- 0x14: CEL data stride field offset\n- 0x20: Hash entry structure offset + flags field offset\n- 0x01: CEL initialization/validity flag bit\n- 0x04: Sprite graphics flag to set\n- 0x40: Loop count for buffer init (64 dwords = 0x100 bytes)",
