      "name": "ProcessCacheBlock",
      "signature": "int ProcessCacheBlock(int nCachePtr, int nSize, int nBlockHandle)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Process cache block with thread-safe critical section locking.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate cache critical section initialized (0x30 offset)\n2. Acquire critical section lock\n3. Check capacity: verify type != 0x1400 and size + offset <= max\n4. If valid, dequeue block from linked list at offset 0x24\n5. If block marked with flag 0x2, skip (in use)\n6. Remove block from doubly-linked list (update next/prev pointers at 0x14, 0x18)\n7. Call FUN_6fe1e410 to process block\n8. If dequeue failed, assert with FogAssertFail\n9. Increment usage counter at offset 0xc\n10. Add size to offset counter at offset 0x8\n11. Release critical section lock\n12. Return dequeued block pointer\n\nParameters:\npCache (ECX) - Pointer to cache structure\nnSize (EDX) - Size to process\nhBlock (Stack) - Block handle/reference\n\nReturns:\nPointer to dequeued block node, or 0 on failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\nReturns 0 if cache not initialized or capacity exceeded\nBlocks marked with flag 0x2 are skipped (in use by other thread)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:f37eae4b9486cb4175333f44901ab791",
