      "name": "DeallocateCacheBlockNode",
      "signature": "int * DeallocateCacheBlockNode(int * pCacheManager, int * pBlockNode, int nSearchCriteria)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Deallocate a cache block node from doubly-linked list and update refcounts\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if cache empty (pCacheManager[0x0c]==0): return NULL if true\n2. If pBlockNode provided, delegate to FUN_6fe1e510 for direct deallocation\n3. If NULL, search cache with FUN_6fe1e490 using nSearchCriteria flag\n4. Validate sprite flags (bit 0x02) and critical section initialized\n5. Enter critical section, decrement cache byte budget by block size\n6. Exit critical section, clear callback and owner references\n7. Insert block into free list: update head/tail or link at tail\n8. Decrement block count, return deallocated block pointer\n\nParameters:\n  pCacheManager (int*): Cache manager structure with block list\n  pBlockNode (int*): Block to deallocate (NULL triggers search)\n  nSearchCriteria (int): Search mode when pBlockNode NULL\n\nReturns:\n  Deallocated block pointer, NULL if cache empty",
