      "name": "UpdateGraphicsCacheMemory",
      "signature": "void UpdateGraphicsCacheMemory(CacheHeader * pCacheHeader, int * pCacheBlock, int nCacheSize, int nReserved)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Update graphics cache memory with new sprite frame data\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if pCacheHeader->pCriticalSection is initialized; fail if NULL\n2. Lock cache using EnterCriticalSection\n3. Load pCacheBlock[1] (current block size/offset)\n4. Subtract block size from pCacheHeader->dwCacheUsed\n5. Add nCacheSize to block offset: pCacheBlock[1] = nCacheSize + old_offset\n6. Set processing flag in pCacheBlock[3] |= 0x02\n7. Calculate new total: pCacheHeader->dwCacheUsed + pCacheBlock[1]\n8. Store in pCacheHeader->dwCacheUsed\n9. Unlock cache using LeaveCriticalSection\n10. If dwCacheTotal exceeds pCacheHeader->dwMaxCacheSize:\n    a. Loop: Call DeallocateCacheBlockNode to free memory\n    b. Break if allocation returns NULL\n    c. Verify freed block is not current pCacheBlock (fail if match)\n    d. Re-lock and recalculate dwCacheTotal\n    e. Continue loop until capacity sufficient\n11. Lock cache, clear flag pCacheBlock[3] &= 0xfffffffd\n12. Unlock cache and return\n\nParameters:\npCacheHeader: CacheHeader* - Cache pool management structure\n  Members: dwMaxCacheSize (0x04), dwCacheUsed (0x08), pCriticalSection (0x30)\npCacheBlock: int* - Block metadata array [dword[4] minimum]\n  [1] = block offset/size\n  [3] = flags (0x02=processing, 0x01=error)\nnCacheSize: int - Bytes to allocate for sprite frame\nnReserved: int - Reserved (unused, pass 0)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Modifies pCacheHeader and pCacheBlock in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\nNULL pCriticalSection triggers assert and exit\nFreed block reallocation (pAllocatedBlock==pCacheBlock) triggers assert and exit\nProcessing flag (0x02) prevents concurrent modification\nPost-update capacity check may reallocate multiple times",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:20dda2e7902f3ba72b8ad8a22afaf82c",
