      "name": "ProcessQueueAndLeaveCriticalSection",
      "signature": "void ProcessQueueAndLeaveCriticalSection(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Fog.LeaveCriticalSection wrapper - Release thread synchronization lock\n\nReleases a critical section lock to allow other threads to access protected data.\nThis is a thin wrapper around the Fog.dll LeaveCriticalSection that processes\npending queue items before releasing the lock.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call ProcessAndClearQueueItems to drain any pending items from g_LinkedListHead\n2. Return (the actual LeaveCriticalSection is handled via thunk tail call)\n\nParameters:\n- None (void signature, uses global g_LinkedListHead)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nRelated Functions:\n- ProcessAndClearQueueItems: Drains the pending item queue\n- Fog.EnterCriticalSection: Corresponding lock acquisition function",
