      "name": "AllocPtListNode",
      "signature": "void AllocPtListNode(uint dwValue1, uint dwValue2)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Allocate and initialize a 108-byte (0x6c) ptList node structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x6c bytes via AllocClientMemory with flags 0\n2. Assert allocation success; terminate on failure\n3. Zero first 4 dwords of structure (offsets 0x0-0xF)\n4. Store dwValue1 at offset 0x0, dwValue2 at offset 0x4\n5. Return node pointer in EAX\n\nParameters:\n- dwValue1 (uint): First value stored at node[0]\n- dwValue2 (uint): Second value stored at node[1]\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to allocated node in EAX (void return type)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x6c (108): PtList node structure size\n- 0x6d (109): Source line number for assert",
