      "name": "AddTileComponentFromImage",
      "signature": "void AddTileComponentFromImage(int * pTile, byte * pbImage, dword dwStride, int nOffsetX, int nOffsetY)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Adds a 32x32 tile component from image data to a tile structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pTile (hTileAdd) and pbImage (ptImage) are not NULL\n2. If tile uses RGB mode (flag 0x2 at offset 0x51):\n   - Scan 32x32 block reading 3 bytes per pixel (RGB)\n   - Compare each pixel against transparency color from tile\n   - If any non-transparent pixel found, goto component creation\n3. If tile uses indexed mode (flag 0x1 at offset 0x51):\n   - Scan 32x32 block reading 1 byte per pixel\n   - If any non-zero (non-transparent) pixel found, goto component creation\n4. Component creation (if non-transparent pixels detected):\n   - Allocate 0x22 (34) byte component struct (ptComp)\n   - Link component into tile's component list at offset 0x58\n   - Increment component count at offset 0x54\n   - Store X/Y offsets as shorts in component (validated < 0x10000)\n   - Allocate 0x118 (280) byte data buffer (ptData), zero-initialize\n   - Set component size to 0xC00, format flags to 0x1001\n   - Copy 32 rows of 96 bytes (0x60) from image with stride\n   - Update tile bounding box (offsets 0x00-0x0C)\n\nParameters:\n- pTile (int*): Tile structure (hTileAdd) to add component to\n- pbImage (byte*): Source image pixel data (ptImage)\n- dwStride (uint): Source image row stride in bytes\n- nOffsetX (int): X offset for component placement\n- nOffsetY (int): Y offset for component placement\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x51: Tile format flags offset (bit 1=RGB, bit 0=indexed)\n- 0x34-0x36: Transparency color bytes (B,G,R)\n- 0x54: Component count offset\n- 0x58: Component list head offset\n- 0x20 (32): Tile dimension in pixels\n- 0x60 (96): Row size in RGB mode (32*3)\n- 0x22 (34): Component structure size\n- 0x118 (280): Component data buffer size\n- 0xC00 (3072): Data size field value (32*32*3)\n- 0x1001: Format/flags field value",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:2b5533b0b1a36c62abd624c360b1163c",
