      "name": "ProcessTileProjectData",
      "signature": "void ProcessTileProjectData(int * pProject, uint * pOutProject, byte * pbDataBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes and processes tile project data structures from serialized format.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate project version equals 7 (TIL format version)\n2. Check flags [EBX+4] bits 0-1; if not both set, exit\n3. Calculate output structure base: [EBX+0x110] = [EBX+0x110] + EBX\n4. Copy string buffer if provided:\n   a. Calculate string length using SCASB loop\n   b. Copy data in 4-byte chunks via MOVSD.REP\n   c. Copy remainder in 1-byte chunks via MOVSB.REP\n5. For each record (count in [EBX+0x10C]):\n   a. Set field [offset+0x58] = pointer to [EBX+8]\n   b. Set field [offset+0x54] = [offset+0x48] + EBX\n   c. For each sub-item in record (count in [offset+0x50]):\n      i. Add EBX to [field+0x10] pointer\n      ii. Accumulate size from word at [field+0xA]\n6. Set flags: clear bit 1, set bit 2 in [EBX+4]\n7. Store base pointer to *pOutProject\n\nParameters:\n- pProject: Pointer to project structure containing TIL format data\n- pOutProject: Output pointer receives processed pProject address\n- pbDataBuffer: Optional data buffer (NULL to skip copy)\n\nReturns:\n- void (always succeeds if version valid, asserts on mismatch)",
