      "name": "InitializeTileProjectData",
      "signature": "void InitializeTileProjectData(int * pProject, int * * ppOutProject, char * szTileData)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initialize tile project data and copy tile definitions into project structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate project version equals 7 (TILEPROJ_DLL_VERSION)\n2. Check if flag 0x02 (processed flag) is set in project flags\n3. Find string length of tile data using REPNE SCASB (count until null terminator)\n4. Calculate inverted string length: ~(count) to get actual byte count\n5. Copy tile data dword-aligned: iterate dwStrLen >> 2 times, copy 4 bytes per iteration\n6. Copy remaining bytes using byte copy loop (dwStrLen & 3 iterations)\n7. For each tile in project:\n   - Set tile pointer at [project_base + 0x58 + (tile_index * 0x60)] to point to copied data\n   - Verify ptCompArray field at [project_base + 0x54] is NULL (assert failure if not)\n   - Verify ptLRUCache field at [project_base + 0x5c] is NULL (assert failure if not)\n   - Increment tile index and advance offset by 0x60\n8. Set flag 0x04 in project flags (mark as initialized)\n9. Write project pointer to output parameter\n\nParameters:\npProject: Pointer to TileProject structure (version field at offset 0, flags at 0x4)\nppProject: Output parameter to receive initialized project pointer\nszTileData: Pointer to tile definition data string (null-terminated)\n\nReturns:\nNone (void function). Success indicated by flag 0x04 set in project flags. Failure causes assert and termination.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If project version != 7, triggers assertion at line 0x37e\n- If any tile's ptCompArray is non-NULL, triggers assertion at line 0x3a1\n- If any tile's ptLRUCache is non-NULL, triggers assertion at line 0x3a2\n- Function uses REPNE SCASB instruction for string length calculation (efficient null scan)\n- Tile structure size is 0x60 bytes\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x37e - Line number in source file (version check assertion)\n0x3a1 - Line number in source file (ptCompArray NULL check assertion)\n0x3a2 - Line number in source file (ptLRUCache NULL check assertion)\n0x4 - Byte offset of flags field in TileProject\n0x44 - Byte offset of relative pointer adjustment field (0x110 offset adjusted)\n0x110 - Byte offset of data pointer field in project structure\n0x43 - Byte offset of tile count field (0x10c relative)\n0x10c - Byte offset of tile count in project structure\n0x54 - Byte offset of ptCompArray field within tile (relative to tile base)\n0x58 - Byte offset of tile pointer field (relative to project + 0x8 base)\n0x5c - Byte offset of ptLRUCache field within tile (relative to tile base)\n0x60 - Size of single tile structure in bytes\n0x02 - Flag mask for \"processed\" flag\n0x04 - Flag mask for \"initialized\" flag\n0xfffffffd - Mask to clear flag 0x02 (AND with this)\n0xffffffff - String length counter init (start as all bits set for REPNE SCASB)\n\nStructure Layout (TileProject):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x0 | 4 | dwVersion | uint | Version code, must equal 7\n0x4 | 4 | dwFlags | uint | Bit 0x02=processed, 0x04=initialized\n0x8+ | N | pTileData | void* | Tile definition data copied here\n0x43 (0x10c) | 4 | nTileCount | int | Number of tiles to initialize\n0x44 (0x110) | 4 | pTileArray | int* | Base pointer to tile array",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:16b397e51bef0ef5a588b4cd82a2578a",
