      "name": "InitializeTileHashTable",
      "signature": "dword * InitializeTileHashTable(int nTileManager)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Initialize hash table for efficient tile lookups.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate and clear buffer for hash table buckets\n2. If allocation fails, assert and terminate via FUN_6fe21293\n3. Verify nTileManager parameter is non-NULL, assert if NULL\n4. Iterate through all tiles in manager (count at offset 0x10C)\n5. For each tile, insert into hash table via InsertTileIntoHashTable\n6. Tile array starts at offset 0x110, stride 0x60 bytes per tile\n7. Return allocated hash table bucket array\n\nParameters:\n  nTileManager (int) - IMPLICIT ECX, pointer to tile manager structure containing tile count (offset 0x10C) and tile array (offset 0x110)\n\nReturns:\n  dword * - pointer to hash table bucket array on success; function terminates on allocation failure or NULL manager",
