      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Search multiple tile arrays for matching tiles via hash table lookup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate ppTileArrays pointer (assert if NULL)\n2. Loop through up to 0x20 (32) tile arrays:\n   a. Break if current array pointer is NULL\n   b. Call FindTileInHashTable for current array\n   c. Accumulate results into pdwResultBuffer\n   d. Return early if dwMaxCount tiles found\n3. Return total tiles found\n\nParameters:\n- ppTileArrays (void**): Array of tile array pointers\n- nSearchParam1-3 (int): Search criteria passed to FindTileInHashTable\n- pdwResultBuffer (uint): Output buffer for tile indices (DWORD array offset)\n- dwMaxCount (uint): Maximum tiles to find\n\nReturns:\n- Total tiles found (dwMaxCount if buffer full, partial count otherwise)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20 (32): Maximum tile arrays to iterate\n- 0x5c (92): Assert line number for NULL check",
