      "name": "GetCallbackIndex",
      "signature": "uint GetCallbackIndex(uint * pData)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Retrieves callback function index from data structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if pData is NULL (zero)\n2. If NULL, invoke Ordinal_10025 with initialization parameters\n3. Dereference pData at offset +8 as unsigned 32-bit value\n4. Return the callback index\n\nParameters:\npData (uint *): Pointer to structure containing callback index. If NULL, triggers initialization via frame buffer setup function.\n\nReturns:\nuint: Callback index value at offset +8 of pData. Used to index into frame buffer callback function table.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL pointer input triggers Ordinal_10025 with hardcoded parameters\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x8 = Offset to callback index field in structure (offset of field at index 2 in uint array)\n0x7f = Third parameter to initialization function (purpose unclear)\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x0    | 4    | [0]        | uint | Magic/type field\n0x4    | 4    | [1]        | uint | Flags field\n0x8    | 4    | [2]        | uint | Callback index (return value of this function)\n0xC    | 4    | [3]        | uint | Reserved/unused",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:edb5e0a82a98a4b8e627f12135ab520c",
