      "name": "DestroyCompressionContext",
      "signature": "void DestroyCompressionContext(void * pContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Destructor for compression context. Initializes vtable, triggers pre-cleanup (0x1b), conditionally deallocates secondary structure at offset +0x04, and triggers post-cleanup (0x1b).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize vtable pointer at context base\n2. Call FUN_6fe21c63(0x1b) for pre-cleanup operations\n3. Load value at context+0x04 into temp register\n4. If temp is non-zero, call FUN_6fe21cd9 with temp as argument\n5. Call FUN_6fe21cc4(0x1b) for post-cleanup operations\n6. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\npContext (void *): Pointer to compression context structure, receives at ECX register (__fastcall)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nNotes:\nCleanup magic number 0x1b (27 decimal) likely encodes cleanup stage or type identifier. Conditional deallocation at offset +0x04 suggests structure contains optional pointer to secondary allocation.",
