      "name": "ExecuteInitializers",
      "signature": "void ExecuteInitializers(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Executes initialization and exit callbacks during program startup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if early initialization callback (PTR_FUN_6fe30ba8) is non-null\n2. If non-null, call early initializer function\n3. Iterate through initialization callback array from g_apInitCallbacksStart to g_apInitCallbacksEnd\n4. For each non-null callback in the array, invoke the function\n5. Iterate through exit callback array from g_apExitCallbacksStart to g_apExitCallbacksEnd\n6. For each non-null callback in exit array, invoke the function\n7. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early initializer callback (PTR_FUN_6fe30ba8) is optional; skipped if null\n- Callback arrays may contain null entries which are skipped during iteration\n- Arrays are defined by inclusive start pointer and exclusive end pointer (similar to C++ iterators)",
