      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Leave critical section 13 (mutex unlock wrapper)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push constant 0xd (13) onto stack as argument\n2. Call FUN_6fe21cc4 which calls LeaveCriticalSection with the passed argument\n3. Return to caller\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: None (void)\n\nPurpose: This is a thin wrapper that leaves critical section 13. Used as a cleanup routine in queue operations and exit handler initialization. The constant 13 refers to a global critical section array index managed elsewhere in the binary.\n\nCalling Function Context:\n- EnqueueItem: Called after enqueuing item to release mutex\n- InitializeExitHandlers: Called during handler initialization",
