      "name": "LeaveCriticalSectionIndex9",
      "signature": "void LeaveCriticalSectionIndex9(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Wrapper function that releases critical section index 9.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push argument 0x9 (critical section index) onto stack\n2. Call LeaveCriticalSectionIndex to release the critical section\n3. Pop ECX (caller cleanup)\n4. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n(none) - Fixed critical section index 9\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- This is a thin wrapper around LeaveCriticalSectionIndex with hardcoded index 9\n- Used for thread synchronization with specific critical section\n- Part of Diablo II's thread synchronization subsystem",
