      "name": "CalculateIndexedValue",
      "signature": "int CalculateIndexedValue(int nOffset, int * pConfig)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Calculate indexed offset-based value from config structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load base value from pConfig[0]\n2. Add nOffset parameter to base value, store in nResult\n3. Load index from pConfig[1]\n4. If index >= 0:\n   a. Load value from pConfig[0] + nOffset (dereferenced as pointer)\n   b. Retrieve additional offset from pConfig[2]\n   c. Load value at (loaded_pointer + pConfig[2])\n   d. Add index to loaded value\n   e. Add combined value to nResult\n5. Return nResult\n\nParameters:\n  int nOffset - Offset value to add to base address\n  int *pConfig - Pointer to config structure containing [base_value, index, offset_value]\n\nReturns:\n  int - Calculated indexed value (base + nOffset) + optional(index + deref_value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If pConfig[1] (index) is negative, skips secondary calculation and returns base + nOffset only\n  - Uses double dereference: follows pointer at (nIndex + nOffset) to get address, then adds offset",
