      "name": "RegisterExceptionHandler",
      "signature": "void RegisterExceptionHandler(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Register C++ exception handler with thread-local storage\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save caller's exception list pointer to stack\n2. Initialize exception frame with -1, handler frame address, and handler entry point\n3. Update thread-local storage to point to new exception frame\n4. Get current TLS context via GetTlsContext() [return: pdwTlsData]\n5. Check if TLS offset +0x60 contains exception handler function pointer\n6. If handler exists (non-zero):\n   - Set state flag to 1 (handler active)\n   - Call GetTlsContext() again to get fresh TLS pointer\n   - Invoke handler function via indirect call through [EAX + 0x60]\n   - Reset state flag to 0 after handler returns\n7. Set final state flag to -1 (exception exit marker)\n8. Jump to exception cleanup routine FUN_6fe25c82\n\nParameters: (none)\n\nReturns: (none - never returns normally, jumps to FUN_6fe25c82)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function does not return; execution transfers to FUN_6fe25c82\n- TLS offset 0x60 must contain valid function pointer for handler invocation\n- FS:[0] register manages thread-local exception chain\n- Note: Function uses EAX register as implicit return for TLS context queries",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:6bbcf292a68b6729c71e4e6b15c80e56",
