      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Validates whether a function pointer points to executable code.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call IsBadCodePtr(pfnCodePtr) to check if pointer is valid\n2. Return true if pointer is valid (IsBadCodePtr returns 0/false)\n3. Return false if pointer is invalid (IsBadCodePtr returns non-zero)\n\nParameters:\n  FARPROC pfnCodePtr - Function pointer to validate\n\nReturns:\n  bool - true if pfnCodePtr is valid executable code, false if invalid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - IsBadCodePtr may raise exceptions; proper exception handling required in caller\n  - NULL pointers are treated as invalid",
