      "name": "CopyMemoryWithOverlapHandling",
      "signature": "void * CopyMemoryWithOverlapHandling(void * pDestination, void * pSource, dword nSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Copy memory with overlap detection and optimized dword-aligned transfer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if pSource < pDestination < (pSource + nSize): if true, detect backward overlap\n2. For backward overlap: align to 4-byte boundary and copy backward using dword ops with REP MOVSD\n3. For no overlap or forward: check if destination is 4-byte aligned\n4. If aligned: split nSize into dword count (nDwordCount = nSize >> 2) and remainder (nRemainder = nSize & 0x03)\n5. If dword count > 7, use dword-aligned loop; otherwise use byte loop\n6. Copy dword-aligned section in 8-dword blocks for cache efficiency\n7. Handle misaligned destination with byte-prefix copies to reach alignment boundary\n8. Copy remaining bytes after main loop (0-3 bytes) based on nRemainder value\n\nParameters:\npDestination (void *): Destination memory address; receives copied data\npSource (void *): Source memory address; data source\nnSize (dword): Number of bytes to copy\n\nReturns:\npDestination on success (always returns param)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Overlapping regions with source above destination: backward copy to prevent corruption\n- Misaligned destination (<4 bytes): align first, then use dword operations\n- Small transfers (<4 bytes): handled with fallthrough byte copy\n- Transfers 4-31 bytes: may use partial dword ops\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x03 - alignment mask for 4-byte boundary check\n0x08 - minimum block size threshold for REP MOVSD\n[EBP + 0x8] - return address restore location",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:bff09423b51fd121ea30afec957819f4",
