      "name": "ClearBitsFromArray",
      "signature": "void ClearBitsFromArray(uint * pBitArray, int nBitIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Clear consecutive bits in a bit array starting from a specified bit position.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate array index: nArrayIndex = nBitIndex / 32 (divide into 32-bit chunks)\n2. Calculate bit mask: nBitMask = 1 << (31 - (nBitIndex % 32))\n3. Clear target bit: Call FUN_6fe27bd5 to clear bit at position nBitIndex\n4. If previous array position exists (nArrayIndex >= 0):\n   - Loop backwards through remaining array elements\n   - Call FUN_6fe27bd5 with bit mask 0x1 to clear all bits\n   - Stop if function returns 0 (success condition met)\n   - Continue until reaching start of array\n\nParameters:\n  pBitArray (uint *) - Pointer to uint array representing bit storage\n  nBitIndex (int) - Starting bit position to clear from\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If nBitIndex points to first element, only clears target bit and returns\n  - Loop continues backwards until reaching array start or function returns 0",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:a1fd1f83ab5d96b4bef4e8817dd3ae88",
