      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Wrapper function that forwards data and configuration to processing function.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push configuration table address (g_adConfigTable) onto stack\n2. Push output result pointer (param_2) onto stack\n3. Push data buffer pointer (param_1) onto stack\n4. Call FUN_6fe261a8 to process data with three parameters\n5. Clean up stack (3 dwords = 12 bytes)\n6. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\npwDataBuffer (ushort *) - Pointer to input data buffer containing resource values\npdwOutputResult (uint *) - Pointer to output result where processed data is stored\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Processing result stored in pdwOutputResult via FUN_6fe261a8\n\nSpecial Cases:\nThis is a thin wrapper that adds the configuration table pointer (g_adConfigTable) as a third parameter to FUN_6fe261a8. The actual processing logic is in the called function.",
