      "name": "PrepareAndProcessData",
      "signature": "void PrepareAndProcessData(void * this, void * pThis, uint * pdwConfig, byte * pbData)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "Helper method: Prepare configuration array and process data through initialization and processing pipeline.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate local 6-element ushort array on stack (size: 12 bytes)\n2. Call FUN_6fe27d76(pThis, &awConfig, &pbData, pbData, 0, 0, 0, 0) to initialize awConfig from pbData input\n3. Call ProcessDataWithConfiguration(awConfig, pdwConfig) to execute main processing with prepared config\n4. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\npThis - Implicit this pointer (stored in ECX), method object instance\npdwConfig - Configuration DWORD array pointer, passed directly to ProcessDataWithConfiguration\npbData - Input data byte buffer pointer, processed by FUN_6fe27d76 to populate awConfig\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, all processing performed via function side effects and output parameters\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- awConfig is stack-allocated temporary, valid only during function execution\n- Both callees may throw exceptions; errors propagate immediately to caller\n- param_2 (pbData) passed both directly and by address to FUN_6fe27d76",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
