      "name": "ProcessCharacterTableWrite",
      "signature": "dword ProcessCharacterTableWrite(dword dwCharIndex, char * szBuffer, dword dwBytesAvailable)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Validates and processes character table entry for buffered write operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if character index is within valid range (< g_dwCharacterTableCount)\n2. Load character table entry from g_pCharacterTableArray indexed by (dwCharIndex >> 5) with stride 0x24\n3. Extract bit 0 from offset +0x04 of character entry to check if character is active (flag 0x01)\n4. If character index invalid OR character flag clear: set error codes and return -1\n5. If character valid and active: call FUN_6fe28620 to prepare processing\n6. Call FUN_6fe26841 to write buffer contents for this character\n7. Call FUN_6fe2867f to finalize processing\n8. Return result from FUN_6fe26841 (bytes written or error code)\n9. If any error: set error codes 9 and 0, return -1\n\nParameters:\ndwCharIndex: Character index to process (0 to g_dwCharacterTableCount-1)\npszBuffer: Pointer to buffer data to write\ndwBytesAvailable: Size of buffer in bytes\n\nReturns:\n>= 0: Success, number of bytes written\n-1: Failure due to invalid character index or inactive character flag\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic Number 0x1f: Extracts lower 5 bits (character index within 32-entry block)\nMagic Number 0x24: Stride between character entries in table (36 bytes)\nMagic Number 0x01: Character active flag (bit 0)\nMagic Number 0x04: Offset to character flags field\nMagic Number 0x05: Stride shift ((dwCharIndex >> 5) = dwCharIndex / 32)\nError Code 9: Invalid character index error\nError Code 0: Success indicator\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fe28620 - Prepare character for processing\n- FUN_6fe26841 - Write character buffer (WriteFile calls, CR/LF conversion)\n- FUN_6fe2867f - Finalize character processing",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
