      "name": "IsCharacterSlotActive",
      "signature": "byte IsCharacterSlotActive(int nSlotIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Return the active/inactive flag (0x40) for a character slot.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if slot index exceeds character table count - return 0 if invalid\n2. Calculate table pointer: g_pCharacterTableArray[slotIndex >> 5]\n3. Calculate record offset: (slotIndex & 0x1f) * 0x24\n4. Load character record byte at offset 4 + record offset\n5. Extract 0x40 flag (active/inactive status)\n\nParameters:\n  dwSlotIndex: Character slot index (0 to character table count - 1)\n\nReturns:\n  0x40: Slot is active\n  0x00: Slot is inactive or index out of bounds\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns 0 if dwSlotIndex >= g_dwCharacterTableCount (invalid slot)\n  - Character records stored in packed array, 0x24 bytes per record\n  - Table array is sparse (32 records per pointer in array)\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n  0x00   | 4    | Header1    | uint | Reserved/header\n  0x04   | 1    | Status     | byte | Status flags (bit 6 = active)\n  0x05   | 35   | Reserved   | byte[35] | Reserved data",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
