      "name": "LeaveCriticalSectionWrap",
      "signature": "void LeaveCriticalSectionWrap(dword pdwHandle)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Dispatch wrapper for leaving critical sections.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load handle from stack parameter\n2. Check if handle within indexed critical section range (0x6fe3307f - 0x6fe332e1)\n3. If within range: calculate 5-bit right-shifted index (subtract base 0x6fe33080, divide by 32, add 0x1c), call LeaveCriticalSectionIndex\n4. If outside range: add 0x20 offset (structure offset to critical section), call LeaveCriticalSection (standard Win32)\n5. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n- pdwHandle (dword): Handle/pointer to either indexed CS header or critical section structure\n\nReturns:\n- void: Always returns normally (both callee paths return)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Range bounds: 0x6fe3307f (exclusive lower) to 0x6fe332e0 (exclusive upper)\n- Magic constants: 0x6fe33080 (base address), 0x901ccf80 (sign extension), 0x1c (index offset), 0x20 (structure field offset)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:ff70d7fac2548b5958f726d1eeb33c1c",
