      "name": "LeaveCriticalSectionDispatcher",
      "signature": "void LeaveCriticalSectionDispatcher(int nIndex, int nCriticalSection)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Dispatcher function to leave critical section using either indexed or direct reference.\n\nAlgorithm\n1. Check if nIndex < 0x14 (20 decimal) - indicates indexed critical section access\n2. If indexed: call LeaveCriticalSectionIndex(nIndex + 0x1c) to leave by index\n3. If not indexed: call LeaveCriticalSection((CRITICAL_SECTION *)(nCriticalSection + 0x20)) to leave by direct pointer\n4. Return void in both paths\n\nParameters\nnIndex - Section index (0-19 for indexed paths, >= 20 for pointer-based paths)\nnCriticalSection - Base address of critical section structure (used when nIndex >= 0x14)\n\nReturns\nvoid - Always returns successfully",
