      "name": "ConvertWideCharToMultiByte",
      "signature": "char * ConvertWideCharToMultiByte(char * szOutput, wchar_t wcChar)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Converts a single wide character to multibyte or ASCII representation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if pszOutput is NULL - return NULL if so\n2. If table mode disabled (g_bTableEnabled = 0):\n   a. Check if wcChar is ASCII (< 0x100)\n   b. If ASCII, write byte directly to output buffer, return 1 (success marker)\n3. If table mode enabled:\n   a. Call WideCharToMultiByte with code page g_dwCodePage (0x220 flags)\n   b. Write character count to stack location [EBP + 0x8] (initially set to 0)\n   c. If conversion succeeded AND no error flag, return converted buffer pointer\n4. On failure:\n   a. Call error handler FUN_6fe2854d() to get error pointer\n   b. Set error code 0x2a (42) at dereferenced pointer\n   c. Return 0xFFFFFFFF (error marker)\n\nParameters:\n- pszOutput (char*): Output buffer for multibyte character\n- wcChar (wchar_t): Wide character to convert\n\nReturns:\n- Success: Pointer to output buffer (converted content) or 1 (ASCII direct write)\n- Failure: 0xFFFFFFFF (error indicator)\n- NULL: If input buffer is NULL\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- ASCII characters (< 0x100) written directly when table mode disabled\n- Wide character conversion uses code page from g_dwCodePage global\n- Error code 0x2a written to output of FUN_6fe2854d() handler\n- Function uses stack parameter for character count (modified via AND [EBP + 0x8], 0)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:12dead7d93dd2763acf5540fd9895c41",
