      "name": "InitializeCharacterTypes",
      "signature": "void InitializeCharacterTypes(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "One-time initialization of character type classification table on first call.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if g_dwInitFlag (static flag) is zero (uninitialized)\n2. If uninitialized, call InitializeCharacterTypeTable with parameter 0xFFFFFFFD\n3. Set g_dwInitFlag to 1 to prevent re-initialization\n4. Return\n\nParameters:\n(none) - uses global g_dwInitFlag as state marker\n\nReturns:\nvoid - always returns on completion\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Parameter 0xFFFFFFFD (-3) passed to InitializeCharacterTypeTable has special meaning in initialization context\n- Safe to call multiple times due to flag guard\n\nRelated Functions:\n- InitializeCharacterTypeTable() - Performs actual classification table initialization\n- ParseGameResourceStrings() - One of the callers that triggers initialization\n- InitializePathBuffers() - Another caller that triggers initialization",
