      "name": "GetStringLengthCapped",
      "signature": "int GetStringLengthCapped(char * szString, int nMaxLength)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Return the length of a string up to a maximum limit, or the limit if not terminated.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize current pointer and remaining count from parameters\n2. If max length is 0, skip to null-terminator check\n3. Loop: decrement remaining count, break if null-terminator found, advance pointer, repeat while count > 0\n4. Check if current position has null-terminator\n5. If null-terminated: return actual string length (pointer difference from start)\n6. If not null-terminated: return input maximum length\n\nParameters:\n- szString: Pointer to input string (may not be null-terminated)\n- nMaxLength: Maximum length to scan (limit on loop iterations)\n\nReturns:\n- Actual string length if null-terminated within nMaxLength\n- nMaxLength if string exceeds limit without null-terminator",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
