      "name": "GetTlsContextOffsetPointer",
      "signature": "dword * GetTlsContextOffsetPointer(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Retrieve TLS context pointer with offset adjustment\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetTlsContext() to retrieve current thread's TLS context base pointer\n2. Add offset of 3 DWORDs (12 bytes = 0xC) to the base pointer\n3. Return the adjusted pointer targeting a specific TLS context field\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nDWORD* - Pointer to TLS context structure adjusted by 3 DWORDs offset\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- GetTlsContext() assumed to never return NULL\n- Fixed offset of 3 DWORDs represents a stable field position within TLS structure\n- Used by multiple character processing functions to access TLS data\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 3: Offset in DWORDs to target field (0xC bytes from base pointer)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:b1691d6b7b8ba065c3fc1a089e8db64e",
