      "name": "FlushCharacterTableWrite",
      "signature": "dword FlushCharacterTableWrite(int * pFileStruct)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Flush buffered writes to character table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if file has pending writes (flags & 0x03 == 0x02 and flags & 0x108 != 0)\n2. Calculate bytes available: *pFileStruct - pFileStruct[2]\n3. If bytes available > 0, write buffered data via ProcessCharacterTableWrite\n4. If write succeeded (bytes written == bytes available):\n   - Clear write flag by AND with 0xfffffffd\n5. If write failed (bytes written != bytes available):\n   - Set error flag (0x20)\n   - Return error code 0xffffffff\n6. Reset buffer management fields: pFileStruct[1] = 0, *pFileStruct = pFileStruct[2]\n7. Return 0 on success or 0xffffffff on failure\n\nParameters:\n  pFileStruct (int *) - Pointer to file structure containing:\n    [0] - Current buffer position/limit\n    [1] - Reserved/temporary field\n    [2] - Buffer start position\n    [3] - Status flags (bits: 0-1=mode, 3=0x08 flag, 7=0x80 flag, 8=0x100 flag)\n    [4] - File handle for writing\n    [7] - Compression buffer (may be NULL)\n\nReturns:\n  0x00000000 - Write succeeded or no pending writes\n  0xffffffff (-1) - Write operation failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Function resets the write buffer position to start after flush\n  - Only flushes if specific flag conditions are met\n  - Gracefully handles zero-byte writes (no-op)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
