      "name": "Mul64",
      "signature": "ulonglong Mul64(uint dwLowA, int nHighA, uint dwLowB, int nHighB)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Multiplies two 64-bit integers represented as low:high 32-bit pairs.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if high parts (nHighA, nHighB) are both zero\n2. If both zero, perform simple 32-bit MUL (dwLowA * dwLowB)\n3. Otherwise compute full 64x64 multiply:\n   result = dwLowA*dwLowB + (nHighA*dwLowB + dwLowA*nHighB) << 32\n\nParameters:\n- dwLowA (uint): Low 32 bits of first operand\n- nHighA (int): High 32 bits of first operand  \n- dwLowB (uint): Low 32 bits of second operand\n- nHighB (int): High 32 bits of second operand\n\nReturns:\n- 64-bit product in EDX:EAX",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
