      "signature": "UnitAny * AllocateAndInsertEntityNode(uint entityId, uint param2, uint param3)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Allocates a new entity node and inserts it at the head of the entity manager's doubly-linked list.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load entity mask value from manager at offset 0x24\n2. Call ProcessEntityPoolSlots to validate or update entity mask value\n3. Re-read mask from manager[9] if validation returned non-zero\n4. Compute slot offset using formula: (entityId & mask) * 12 bytes per entity\n5. Call virtual allocator function at vftable[1] with computed slot address\n6. Use allocated result if successful, otherwise use default node at manager[2]\n7. Check if node currently has existing links by testing next pointer at offset 0\n8. If node is already linked, unlink it from current position:\n   - Load previous pointer at offset 4\n   - Decode negative offset using NOT if sign bit set\n   - Compute positive offset relative to current node if positive\n   - Update previous node's next pointer to skip current node\n   - Update next node's previous pointer to skip current node\n   - Clear both forward and backward pointers on node\n9. Insert node at head of list:\n   - Load current list head from manager[2]\n   - Set new node's next pointer to current head\n   - Set new node's previous pointer to head's previous pointer\n   - Update current head's previous pointer to reference new node\n   - Update manager's head reference to new node\n10. Store entityId in node's dwType field (offset 0) and return node pointer\n\nParameters:\n  entityId: Entity ID to assign to node; masked with manager's dwEntityMask\n  param2: First parameter passed to virtual allocator function\n  param3: Second parameter passed to virtual allocator function\n\nImplicit Parameter (passed in EDI register):\n  pEntityManager: Pointer to entity manager structure\n\nReturns:\n  EAX: Pointer to allocated UnitAny node; always non-NULL (uses default if allocation fails)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Entity mask may be updated by ProcessEntityPoolSlots; uses reloaded value\n  - Allocation failure at 0x262f falls back to default node at offset 8 from manager\n  - Handles relinking of entities already in list; unlinks before reinsertion\n  - Supports both positive and negative offset encodings in previous pointer field\n  - Stride calculation for pool slots is always 12 bytes per entity\n  - Virtual function call at 0x262a uses standard __thiscall convention with ECX = manager\n\nStructure Layout (Entity Manager):\n  Offset  | Size | Field Name   | Type      | Description\n  --------|------|--------------|-----------|----------------------------------------\n  +0x00   | 4    | vftable      | void*     | Virtual function table for allocation\n  +0x04   | 4    | offsetAdj    | int       | Offset adjustment added to allocations\n  +0x08   | 4    | listHead     | UnitAny*  | Head of doubly-linked entity list\n  +0x1C   | 4    | poolBase     | void*     | Base address of entity pool storage\n  +0x24   | 4    | dwEntityMask | uint      | Mask for entity ID slot calculation",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.12a",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:3fffa0aa9336cb6abefa0682ac1ac9d8",
