      "name": "CalculateNextValidCapacity",
      "signature": "uint CalculateNextValidCapacity(int * pPoolManager)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Validates and normalizes capacity value for entity pool allocation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if proposedCapacity < 0x15 (21):\n   a. Calculate bitPattern = (proposedCapacity - 1) AND proposedCapacity\n   b. Loop: Clear lowest set bit iteratively until bitPattern becomes zero\n      - Move bitPattern to current iteration variable\n      - Calculate new bitPattern = (current - 1) AND current\n      - Continue while bitPattern != 0\n   c. If proposedCapacity == 0 after bit clearing, it's a power of 2\n   d. Return 1 if valid power of 2, or proposedCapacity if not\n2. If proposedCapacity >= 0x15:\n   a. Write maximum value 0x15 to pPoolManager[3] (offset +0xC)\n   b. Return 0x15 (capped capacity)\n3. Return the final capacity value\n\nParameters:\n  proposedCapacity (EAX, implicit): Proposed capacity value to validate\n    Must be a power of 2 for valid allocation (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n    Maximum allowed value is 0x15 (21 decimal)\n  pPoolManager: Pointer to pool manager structure\n    Offset +0xC: Capacity field updated when proposedCapacity >= 0x15\n\nReturns:\n  uint: Validated/normalized capacity value\n    Returns 1 if proposedCapacity is valid power of 2 (< 0x15)\n    Returns 0x15 if proposedCapacity >= 0x15 (capped to maximum)\n    Returns proposedCapacity if not a valid power of 2\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Magic value 0x15: Maximum pool capacity (21 decimal)\n  - Bit manipulation loop: (value - 1) AND value clears the lowest set bit\n  - Power of 2 detection: Only single-bit values pass validation (1,2,4,8,16)\n  - Side effect: Modifies pPoolManager[3] when capacity exceeds maximum\n  - Input constraint: Capacity must be power of 2 or validation fails\n  - Calling convention: __stdcall with 4-byte parameter cleanup",
